40431742,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,pro and RT,"HIV-1 resistance genotyping was used for the identification of RAMs in the HIV-1 polymerase (pol) gene. The final PCR product was 1084 base pairs in length, encompassing the protease and reverse-transcriptase regions of the HIV-1 pol gene.",The paper mentions the sequencing of the protease and reverse-transcriptase regions of the HIV-1 pol gene.
40431742,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Argentina,"This study analyzed genotype results gathered from plasma samples drawn as part of routine clinical practice from naïve adult PLWHA from two reference HIV-clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina.","The paper specifies that the samples were obtained from two reference HIV clinics in Buenos Aires, Argentina."
40431742,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2017-2021,A cross-sectional study was undertaken utilizing samples collected between 2017 and 2021 at two reference HIV clinics.,The paper states that the samples were collected between 2017 and 2021.
40431742,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"The amplified PCR products were sequenced using four primers. The sequencing products were analyzed on an Applied Biosystems/Hitachi 3500 Genetic Analyzer (Waltham, MA, USA).","The paper describes the use of an Applied Biosystems/Hitachi 3500 Genetic Analyzer for sequencing, which is consistent with Sanger sequencing."
40431742,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"In the first round of PCR, the primers PRTMF1 (5'-ATGAARGATTGYACRAGRCAGGCTAAT3') and RTR1 (5'-ATCCCTGCATAAATCTGACTTGC-3') were used. The second round of PCR utilized the primers PRT-F2 (5'-CTTTARCTTCCCTCARATCACTCT-3') and RTR2 (5'-CTTCTGTATGTCATTGACAGTCC-3'). For sequencing, four primers were employed: the second-round PCR primers PRT-F2 and RTR2, along with two additional internal primers, SeqF4 (5'-CAGTACTGGATGTGGGRGAYG-3') and SeqR4 (5'-TACTAGGTATGGTAAATGCAGT-3').",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
40431742,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"All plasma samples were processed and stored for the determination of drug resistance mutations at the Laboratorio Dr. Stamboulian molecular biology division in Buenos Aires, Argentina, according to standardized procedures. Briefly, HIV-1 resistance genotyping was used for the identification of RAMs in the HIV-1 polymerase (pol) gene. 4620. The existence of a genotypic resistance test was the starting point for the development of the study. An anonymized list of genotypes in the naïve HIV-1 population was extracted and, based on laboratory ID coding/number, records were matched with the clinical records database in both institutions for extraction of aggregated clinical and epidemiological data.",The paper specifies that plasma samples were used for sequencing.
40431742,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"Treatment-naive, defined as no antiretrovirals (in combination or monotherapy) received before resistance test based on clinical records.","The paper defines the study population as treatment-naive individuals, meaning they had not received any antiretrovirals before the resistance test."
