40490983,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"We conducted a retrospective cohort study of people living with HIV (PLWH) ≥ 3 years old with second-line viral failure (VF, ≥ 1000 copies/ml) at the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare from 2011 to 2021. Genotyping was recommended after confirmed second-line failure.","The paper mentions the study includes PLWH who underwent genotyping, indicating HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
40490983,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"Methods: We conducted a retrospective cohort study of people living with HIV (PLWH)  3	excl  years old with second-line viral failure (VF,  1000  copies/ml) at the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare from 2011 to 2021. We assessed resistance prevalence and patterns at second-line VF, stratified by PI (atazanavir/ritonavir or lopinavir/ritonavir), and examined correlations of resistance and treatment strategies with VF at 6-18 months post-genotype. Analyses employed inverse probability weighting, adjusting for calendar year, age, gender, ART duration, PI at genotyping and class-specific resistance, and considered guidelines-supported versus unsupported strategies.",The paper focuses on resistance prevalence and patterns in patient samples rather than in vitro drug susceptibility testing.
40490983,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,None,No evidence,The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
40490983,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Protease and reverse transcriptase,Protease and reverse transcriptase resistance mutations were obtained from sequences requested from laboratories.,"The paper mentions that protease and reverse transcriptase resistance mutations were obtained from sequences, indicating these genes were sequenced."
40490983,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Kenya,"We conducted a retrospective cohort study of people living with HIV (PLWH)  3	excl  years old with second-line viral failure (VF,  1000  copies/ml) at the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare from 2011 to 2021. The study was conducted in Kenya, at the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare (AMPATH).","The paper states the study was conducted in Kenya, and the samples were obtained from this country."
40490983,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2011 to 2021,A total of 254 second-line failure genotypes were ordered at AMPATH from 2011 to 2021 (Figure 1).,"The paper mentions the samples were obtained from 2011 to 2021, covering a ten-year period."
40490983,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,Sanger sequencing of plasma HIV-1 RNA was performed by the Kisumu Kenya Medical Research Institute and Nairobi National HIV Reference Laboratories.,"The paper mentions that Sanger sequencing of plasma HIV-1 RNA was performed by two laboratories, indicating this method was used for sequencing."
40490983,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,No evidence,The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
40490983,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma HIV-1 RNA,Sanger sequencing of plasma HIV-1 RNA was performed by the Kisumu Kenya Medical Research Institute and Nairobi National HIV Reference Laboratories.,The paper specifies that plasma HIV-1 RNA was sequenced.
40490983,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"We conducted a retrospective cohort study of people living with HIV (PLWH)  3	excl  years old with second-line viral failure (VF,  1000  copies/ml) at the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare from 2011 to 2021.","The paper focuses on individuals with second-line viral failure, indicating sequences were obtained from such individuals."
40490983,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"We conducted a retrospective cohort study of people living with HIV (PLWH)  3	excl  years old with second-line viral failure (VF,  1000  copies/ml) at the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare from 2011 to 2021.",The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial.
40490983,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,187,"Thus, 187 PLWH with genotypes were analysed, with a median age at genotyping 41 years and 54% female (Table 1).",The paper states that 187 individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing.
40490983,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"We conducted a retrospective cohort study of people living with HIV (PLWH)  3	excl  years old with second-line viral failure (VF,  1000  copies/ml) at the Academic Model Providing Access to Healthcare from 2011 to 2021. Of 187 participants,  7	excl  had intermediate-high resistance to ≥ 1 regimen drug at genotyping (76% NRTIs, 34% PIs, 34% dual-class).","The paper mentions the study involved PLWH with second-line failure, all of whom had received ARV, and the study also mentioned characteristics in patients who are on ARV, which indicated sequences were obtained from these individuals."
40490983,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI, PI","Of 187 participants,  7	excl  had intermediate-high resistance to ≥ 1 regimen drug at genotyping (76% NRTIs, 34% PIs, 34% dual-class).","The paper mentions resistance to NRTI, NNRTI, and PI, indicating these drug classes were received before sequencing."
40490983,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Efavirenz, Nevirapine, Atazanavir, Lopinavir","During the study, recommended anchor drugs for first-line regimens included efavirenz or nevirapine for individuals ≥ 3 years; second-line regimens included atazanavir/ritonavir or lopinavir/ritonavir plus two NRTIs.","The paper mentions the specific drugs recommended for use, including efavirenz, nevirapine, atazanavir, and lopinavir."
40490983,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,The data that support the findings of this study are available from the corresponding author upon reasonable request.,"The paper states the data are available upon request, which indicates that the sequences are not publicly available."
40573423,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,We provide a comprehensive overview of the HIV-1 genetic distribution and TDR patterns in South Korea from 2021 to 2024.,"The study focuses on analyzing the genetic distribution and transmitted drug resistance patterns of HIV-1 among individuals in South Korea, indicating that patient samples were sequenced."
40573423,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,The study does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility testing or data.,"The focus is on transmitted drug resistance mutations in patient samples, not on in vitro susceptibility."
40573423,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not reported,The paper does not provide specific GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.,There is no mention of GenBank accession numbers in the provided text.
40573423,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"env, gag, pol, protease, reverse transcriptase, integrase","Reverse transcription and nested PCR were performed to amplify the envelope (env), gag protein (gag), and pol protein (pol) for genotyping and the protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase genes for drug resistance analysis.","Multiple genes including env, gag, pol, protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase were sequenced for both genotyping and drug resistance analysis."
40573423,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,South Korea,This study investigated the proportion of transmitted drug resistance (TDR) mutations and human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-1 subtypes among 487 antiretroviral therapy (ART)-naïve individuals in South Korea from 2021 to 2024.,Samples were obtained from individuals diagnosed with HIV in South Korea.
40573423,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2021 to 2024,"The initial diagnosis for all included PWH was made between January 2021 and October 2024. The study included 487 PWH: 99 from 2021, 143 from 2022, 148 from 2023, and 97 from 2024.",The study covers a period from 2021 to 2024.
40573423,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,Sanger sequencing was performed using in-house sequencing primers. Sequence quality and the generated consensus sequence alignments were assessed using Geneious Prime software version 2025.,The paper specifies that Sanger sequencing was used for the study.
40573423,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.,There is no mention of cloning in the provided text.
40573423,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma or serum,"Viral RNA was extracted from 140  micro;L of plasma or serum using the QIAcube extraction system (QIAGEN, Hilden, Germany), according to the manufacturer's instructions.",The paper specifies that viral RNA was extracted from plasma or serum samples.
40573423,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,Recently diagnosed PWH who had not been exposed to ART were included.,The study included only treatment-naive individuals.
40573423,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial.,There is no mention of a clinical trial in the provided text.
40573423,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,487,"The study included 487 PWH: 99 from 2021, 143 from 2022, 148 from 2023, and 97 from 2024.",The paper states that 487 individuals were included in the study.
40573423,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,Recently diagnosed PWH who had not been exposed to ART were included.,The study included only treatment-naive individuals.
40573423,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,Recently diagnosed PWH who had not been exposed to ART were included.,The study included only treatment-naive individuals.
40573423,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,Recently diagnosed PWH who had not been exposed to ART were included.,The study included only treatment-naive individuals.
40573423,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,Data Availability Statement: The data used to support this study are available from the corresponding author upon request.,"The sequences were not made publicly available, but were available from the corresponding author upon request."
40596906,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health (GenBank accession number PV526713-PV526742).","The paper reports genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region obtained from patient samples, specifically from mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1."
40596906,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,No evidence.,The study focuses on genotypic sequences and resistance mutations without discussing in vitro drug susceptibility assays or results.
40596906,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,PV526713-PV526742,"Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health (GenBank accession number PV526713-PV526742).","The paper provides the range of GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, specifically PV526713 to PV526742."
40596906,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,pol (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT),"Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health (GenBank accession number PV526713-PV526742).","The paper mentions the sequencing of the pol region, which includes the protease and reverse transcriptase genes."
40596906,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Brazil,"The study was conducted from October 2021 to September 2023 in São Luís, Maranhão, and Recife, Pernambuco, at the High-Risk Maternity Hospital in Imperatriz, Pediatric Infectious Disease Outpatient Clinic at the University Hospital of the Federal University of Maranhão, and Pediatric Infectious Disease Outpatient Clinic at the University Hospital Oswaldo Cruz of the University of Pernambuco.","The paper specifies that the study was conducted in Brazil, specifically in the Northeast region, including Maranhão and Pernambuco."
40596906,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2007–2022,"This study aimed to describe the transmission of drug-resistant HIV-1 variants and phylogenetic characterisation of viral strains in mother-child pairs from the cities of Recife and São Luís, located in the Northeast region of Brazil, in 2007–2022. This study was conducted from October 2021 to September 2023 in São Luís, Maranhão, and Recife, Pernambuco, at the High-Risk Maternity Hospital in Imperatriz, Pediatric Infectious Disease Outpatient Clinic at the University Hospital of the Federal University of Maranhão, and Pediatric Infectious Disease Outpatient Clinic at the University Hospital Oswaldo Cruz of the University of Pernambuco.",The paper mentions the study period as 2007 to 2022 for the data collection and 2021 to 2023 for the study.
40596906,7,What method was used for sequencing?,ViroSeq Genotyping System,"Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health (GenBank accession number PV526713-PV526742).","The paper specifies the use of the ViroSeq Genotyping System for obtaining the genotypic sequences, which is a method used for sequencing HIV."
40596906,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"The genotyping sequences were provided by the Brazilian Ministry of Health. The analyses included descriptions of antiretroviral resistance mutation profiles of the mothers and children, subtype determination, and phylogenetic analyses.  The analyses included descriptions of antiretroviral resistance mutation profiles of the mothers and children, subtype determination, and phylogenetic analyses.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing. It describes the direct sequencing of HIV genotypic sequences.
40596906,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,HIV pol region from blood samples,"Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health (GenBank accession number PV526713-PV526742).","The paper indicates that genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region were obtained, typically from blood samples."
40596906,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,The mothers included both treatment-naive women diagnosed during pregnancy who underwent pretreatment genotyping and those living with HIV-1 during prior treatment who required genotyping due to virological failure.,The paper mentions that some mothers were living with HIV-1 during prior treatment who required genotyping due to virological failure.
40596906,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"Methods This study included 15 mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1. The genotyping sequences were provided by the Brazilian Ministry of Health. The analyses included descriptions of antiretroviral resistance mutation profiles of the mothers and children, subtype determination, and phylogenetic analyses",The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial. It describes a study conducted on mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1.
40596906,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,15,This study included 15 mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1. The mothers included both treatment-naive women diagnosed during pregnancy who underwent pretreatment genotyping and those living with HIV-1 during prior treatment who required genotyping due to virological failure.,The paper states that the study included 15 mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1.
40596906,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"Methods This study included 15 mother-child pairs with confirmed vertical transmission of HIV-1. The genotyping sequences were provided by the Brazilian Ministry of Health. The analyses included descriptions of antiretroviral resistance mutation profiles of the mothers and children, subtype determination, and phylogenetic analyses",The paper mentions some mothers living with HIV-1 during prior treatment who required genotyping due to virological failure. From the children nine had received and three had not received ARV drugs before sample sequencing.
40596906,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, PI, NNRTI","Among the 15 study pairs, ten children (66.7%) started ART within the first two years of life. Of the nine children who had initiated ART, three (20%), two (13.3%) and two (6.7%) received zidovudine (ZDV) + lamivudine (3TC) + nevirapine (NVP), ZDV + 3TC + lopinavir/ritonavir, or ZDV + 3TC + efavirenz (EFV), respectively. <br Mother-child pairs 1, 2, 5, and 7 received the same ART regimen (ZDV + 3TC + NVP). Mothers 3, 6, 8, 9, and 15 received EFV-based regimens.  Of the nine children who had initiated ART, three (20%), two (13.3%) and two (6.7%) received zidovudine (ZDV) + lamivudine (3TC) + nevirapine (NVP), ZDV + 3TC + lopinavir/ritonavir, or ZDV + 3TC + efavirenz (EFV), respectively.","The paper mentions the use of NRTI (ZDV, 3TC), PI (lopinavir/ritonavir), and NNRTI (NVP, EFV) before sample sequencing."
40596906,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"3TC, ZDV, NVP, EFV, LPV/r","Of the nine children who had initiated ART, three (20%) received zidovudine (ZDV) + lamivudine (3TC) + nevirapine (NVP), two (13.3%) received ZDV + 3TC + lopinavir/ritonavir, and two (6.7%) received ZDV + 3TC + efavirenz (EFV) <br Mother-child pairs 1, 2, 5, and 7 received the same ART regimen (ZDV + 3TC + NVP). Mothers 3, 6, 8, 9, and 15 received EFV-based regimens.","The paper lists the specific drugs received by individuals, including zidovudine (ZDV), lamivudine (3TC), nevirapine (NVP), efavirenz (EFV), and lopinavir/ritonavir (LPV/r)."
40596906,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,"Genotypic sequences of the HIV pol region (protease/reverse transcriptase-PR/RT) were obtained using the ViroSeq Genotyping System, carried out in the laboratories of the National Genotyping Network (RENAGENO) coordinated by the Department of HIV/AIDS of the Brazilian Ministry of Health (GenBank accession number PV526713-PV526742).","The paper provides GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates, indicating that the sequences were made publicly available."
