40713598,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Frozen plasma samples were shipped on dry ice to the Virology Quality Assurance-approved laboratory.,"Briefly, frozen plasma samples were shipped on dry ice to the Virology Quality Assurance-approved laboratory [9] at the Providence-Boston Center for AIDS Research Laboratory.",The paper specifies that frozen plasma samples were used for sequencing.
40713598,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,The study described HIV drug resistance among 20 children and adolescents with virologic failure on non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)-based therapy.,"HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) was retrospectively characterized among 20 children and adolescents with HIV with virologic failure on non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)-based therapy, and virologic response in those switched to dolutegravir (DTG)-based therapy described. All participants had at least one NNRTI resistance mutation, most commonly K103N (N = 12) and 15 (75%) had nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) resistance mutations, most commonly M184I/V (N = 15). Five (45%) of 11 participants who were switched to DTG-based regimens for a median of 50 months had HIV suppression.",The paper states that the study included participants with virologic failure on NNRTI-based therapy.
40713598,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Participants included CAWH from a previous study that examined the virologic response to NNRTI-based ART from the Pediatric HIV/AIDS Care Program at Korle-Bu Teaching Hospital in Ghana.,Participants included CAWH from a previous study that examined the virologic response to NNRTI-based ART from the Pediatric HIV/AIDS Care Program at Korle-Bu Teaching Hospital in Ghana [8].,The paper does not mention that the patients were part of a clinical trial; they were receiving standard care.
40713598,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,20,Twenty samples were successfully amplified and sequenced (Figure S1).,The paper states that twenty samples were successfully amplified and sequenced.
40713598,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) was retrospectively characterized among 20 children and adolescents with HIV with virologic failure on non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)-based therapy, and virologic response in those switched to dolutegravir (DTG)-based therapy described. All participants had at least one NNRTI resistance mutation, most commonly K103N (N = 12) and 15 (75%) had nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) resistance mutations, most commonly M184I/V (N = 15)","HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) was retrospectively characterized among 20 children and adolescents with HIV with virologic failure on non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)-based therapy, and virologic response in those switched to dolutegravir (DTG)-based therapy described. All participants had at least one NNRTI resistance mutation, most commonly K103N (N = 12) and 15 (75%) had nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) resistance mutations, most commonly M184I/V (N = 15).",The paper mentions participants had at least one NRTI resistance which indicates they had previously received ARV drugs.
40713598,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,NRTIs and NNRTIs,"HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) was retrospectively characterized among 20 children and adolescents with HIV with virologic failure on non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NNRTI)-based therapy, and virologic response in those switched to dolutegravir (DTG)-based therapy described. All participants had at least one NNRTI resistance mutation, most commonly K103N (N = 12) and 15 (75%) had nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI) resistance mutations, most commonly M184I/V (N = 15)","The paper discusses resistance to nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs) and non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTIs), indicating those drug classes were received."
40713598,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Abacavir, Lamivudine, Zidovudine, Efavirenz, Nevirapine",The ART regimen at the time of failure is shown in Table S1. Fifteen participants (75%) had CRF02_AG (Table S1),"The paper provides specific drug regimens received at virological failure, including Abacavir, Lamivudine, Zidovudine, Efavirenz, Nevirapine."
