40763144,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,The data used in this study is available on the Ugandan Ministry of Health HIV Drug Resistance Database but is not publicly accessible due to patient confidentiality policies. Access may be granted upon request to the Ugandan Ministry of Health.,The paper states that the data used in the study is not publicly accessible due to patient confidentiality policies.
40779404,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"Preexisting K65R/N mutations were detected in 20 of 2028 VS participants who received B/F/TAF. Of the 20 participants with K65R/N, all had proviral DNA genotyping data available at BL and 7 had historical RNA genotype data.","The paper mentions the detection of preexisting K65R/N mutations in participants, which indicates that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
40779404,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"HIV-1 drug resistance affects antiretroviral treatment options for people with HIV-1 (PWH); however, limited clinical data are available regarding the impact of preexisting K65R/N on B/F/TAF regimen efficacy.  Maximum reductions in viral load in 277 participants were 1.5-fold and 1.6-fold for K65R and K65N, respectively, compared with those without K65R/N mutations which is a limited clinical data.",The paper focuses on clinical outcomes and genotypic analyses rather than in vitro drug susceptibility testing.
40779404,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,,No GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates were provided in the paper.,The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
40779404,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"Protease, RT, IN","We collected historical RNA or proviral DNA genotyping reports for protease (PR), RT, and integrase (IN), from local laboratories or commercial sites if available. Retrospective proviral DNA genotyping of PR/RT/IN using GenoSure Archive (Monogram Biosciences, CA), which uses NGS technology was performed on BL whole blood samples.","The paper mentions the sequencing of the protease, RT, and integrase genes for genotypic analyses."
40779404,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,United States,No specific countries were mentioned as the paper focused on clinical trial participants.,The paper did not specify the countries from which the sequenced samples were obtained.
