40779404,7,What method was used for sequencing?,NGS,"Retrospective proviral DNA genotyping of PR/RT/IN using GenoSure Archive (Monogram Biosciences, CA), which uses NGS technology was performed on BL whole blood samples.",The paper mentions the use of NGS technology for genotyping.
40779404,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"Retrospective proviral DNA genotyping of PR/RT/IN using GenoSure Archive (Monogram Biosciences, CA), which uses NGS technology was performed on BL whole blood samples.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
40779404,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Whole blood,"Retrospective proviral DNA genotyping of PR/RT/IN using GenoSure Archive (Monogram Biosciences, CA), which uses NGS technology was performed on BL whole blood samples.",The paper specifies that whole blood samples were used for genotyping.
40779404,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"All participants with preexisting K65R/N receiving B/F/TAF (n = 20/20) had virologic suppression (HIV-1 RNA < 50 copies/mL) through end of study, with no virologic failure or treatment-emergent resistance to B/F/TAF.","The paper states that all participants had virologic suppression, indicating no virological failure."
40779404,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Yes,"This is a post hoc analysis evaluating virologic outcomes of participants with K65R/N receiving B/F/TAF across 6 Phase 2/3/3b studies. The trial designs were as follows: Studies 1844 and 4030 were double-blinded placebo controlled, Studies 1878 and 4580 were randomized open-label, and Studies 1474 and 4449 were single-arm open label.",The paper mentions the study was a post hoc analysis of 6 phase 2/3/3b trials.
40779404,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,2028,"From the 2182 participants who received B/F/TAF, 2028 participants had BL genotypic RT data.",The paper states that 2028 participants had baseline genotypic RT data.
40779404,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"Preexisting HIV-1 drug resistance affects antiretroviral treatment options for people with HIV-1 (PWH). All participants with preexisting K65R/N were virologically suppressed on ART with a median time on ART before study entry of 9.2 years (range 1.6-26.3 years). Frequencies of K65R/N mutations over 1% and the TFV RAMs that confer resistance were present in the study.  The observed frequencies of K65R/N are similar to prior studies in virologically suppressed                                                                              (VS) participants with preexisting K65R/N who received B/F/TAF in the OLE phase or 104 weeks. K65R/N is less likely to emerge in people who are virologically suppressed (VS) on tenofovir without a switch to a very short-acting potent integrase inhibitor (INSTI) with high resistance barrier, like B/F/TAF; hence the mean of 9 years on ART before this study;  Or one ongoing prep study with the K65R emerging due but they didn’t switch to shorter acting and potent regimen like TAF based INSTI system so no comparison of vs people K65R—-outcome TFV vs no TFV effectiveness. And they randomized K65R/N, which reflects more real-life clinical situations for B/F/TAF; that’s why K65R/N are so rare; not done for other tenofovir studies. Theoretically preexisting K65R and M184I/V + TDF population switch to B/F/TAF study should demonstrate virologic failure to 50-80% so make this study rational and meaningful.","The paper mentions drug history of the 20 participants with preexisting K65R/N were collected: In total, 20 participants with preexisting K65R/N were identified across 6 B/F/TAF clinical trials and analyzed in this post hoc study (1.0% of all participants who received B/F/TAF). The participants with preexisting K65R/N were predominantly treated in the USA, and 13 were randomized to B/F/TAF, and 7 were randomized to comparator. All the 7 comparator arm participants had virologic success at study time points (Week 24, Week 48) before switching to B/F/ TAF in the OLE phase. These data and patient characteristics of 20 preexisting K65R/N participants are distinct from those of the nested study cohort to elucidate whether presence of K65R/N before initiation of B/F/TAF affects virologic outcome in a post hoc manner."
40779404,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTIs, NNRTs, PIs, INSTIs","Before enrollment, participants had been treated with TFV (80.0%), INSTIs (50.0%), non-nucleoside RT inhibitors (NNRTI; 45.0%), and PR inhibitors (PI; 75.0%).","The paper lists the drug classes received by participants before enrollment, including NRTIs, NNRTIs, PIs, and INSTIs."
40779404,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF), Tenofovir alafenamide fumarate (TAF), Integrase strand transfer inhibitors (INSTIs), Non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTIs), Protease inhibitors (PIs)","Before enrollment, participants had been treated with Tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF) (80.0%), INSTIs (50.0%), non-nucleoside RT inhibitors (NNRTI; 45.0%), and PR inhibitors (PI; 75.0%).","The paper specifies the drugs received by participants before sequencing, including TDF and TAF, NNRTIs, PIs, and INSTIs."
