40857111,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"Yes, the patients were part of a clinical trial (the ALLIANCE study).",The design of the phase 3 randomized ALLIANCE study (GS-US-380-4458; NCT03547908) has been described previously.,The paper describes the study as part of the phase 3 randomized ALLIANCE study.
40857111,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,"22 participants had postbaseline HIV-1 resistance testing. In total 208 participants received ≥1 dose of B/F/TAF in either phase and had ≥1 on-treatment, postbaseline HIV-1 RNA and HBV DNA result","In total, 22 participants met the criteria for postbaseline HIV-1 resistance testing, and data were available for ≥1 gene for 19 (86%) of these participants.",The paper mentions that resistance testing was performed for 22 participants.
40857111,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,"Yes, the paper reports sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.","Participants could enter a 48-week open-label B/F/TAF-only phase. This subanalysis reports HIV-1 resistance results to the end of masked treatment. 208 participants received ≥1 dose of B/F/TAF in either phase and had ≥1 on-treatment, postbaseline HIV-1 RNA and HBV DNA result. In this analysis of the ALLIANCE study, high rates of virologic suppression were maintained to the end of the study, including ≥96 weeks of masked treatment with B/F/TAF or DTG+F/TDF and 48 weeks of open-label treatment with B/F/TAF.",The participants received treatment in the ALLIANCE study before the samples were obtained for sequencing.
40857111,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs) and integrase inhibitors (INSTIs) were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing.,"After the 96-week randomized phase of ALLIANCE, participants could enter a 48-week open-label B/F/TAF-only phase. The study design was described previously: The 48-week open label extension (OLE) phase followed in which all participants could receive B/F/TAF or switch from dolutegravir (DTG) plus tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (TDF) plus emtricitabine (FTC) to B/F/TAF.","The paper mentions the use of NRTIs and INSTIs, but does not mention  whether or not PIs and NNRTIs were used."
40857111,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Bictegravir/emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (B/F/TAF) or dolutegravir plus emtricitabine/tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (DTG+F/TDF) were received.,ALLIANCE is a phase 3 randomized study of bibtegravir/emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (B/F/TAF) versus dolutegravir + emtricitabine/tenofovir disoproxil fumarate (DTG+F/TDF) in treatment-naive people with HIV-1/hepatitis B virus (HBV) coinfection.,The paper mentions that participants received either B/F/TAF or DTG+F/TDF.
40857111,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"No, the paper does not mention that the sequences were made publicly available.",No evidence,The paper does not mention any public availability of the sequences.
40872801,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.",The paper is a systematic review and meta-analysis and does not report original sequences from patient samples.
40872801,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"The systematic literature search was carried out between February and March 2025 on online databases including MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL, while Google Scholar was used to identify grey literature and would not be identified by other databases.",The paper focuses on drug resistance mutations and HIV-1 subtypes but does not mention in vitro drug susceptibility data.
40872801,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.",The paper does not provide GenBank accession numbers as it does not report original sequencing data.
40872801,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.",The paper does not report original sequencing data or specific HIV genes sequenced.
40872801,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.","The paper is a systematic review and meta-analysis, focusing on studies in Tanzania."
40872801,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,No,"A total of 9685 HIV patients from 23 eligible studies were analyzed. The prevalence of virological failure in studies that used a threshold of >1000 and >400 copies/mL was 24.83% (95% CI: 17.85-32.53%) and 36.94% (95% CI: 24.79-50.00%), respectively. Major DRMs were observed at 87.61% (95% CI: 76.25-95.91%). A decrease in prevalence was observed in studies conducted from 2019, with a pooled prevalence of 62.15% (95% CI: 31.57-88.33%). The most frequently observed HIV-1 subtypes were subtype C at 36.20% (95% CI: 30.71-41.85%), A1 at 33.13% (95% CI: 28.23-38.20%), and subtype D at 16.00% (95% CI: 11.41-21.12%), while recombinant forms of the virus were observed at 13.29% (95% CI: 9.79-17.17%). The prevalence of DRMs against NRTIs and NNRTIs was significantly high, while that against INSTIs and PIs was low, supporting the continued use of PI- and INSTI-based regimens in Tanzania and the need for continued surveillance of DRMs.",Samples were collected from studies  conducted from 2004 to 2024.
40872801,7,What method was used for sequencing?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.","The paper does not report on sequencing methods, as it does not present original sequencing data."
40872801,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
40872801,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.",The paper does not report any clinical specimens as it focuses on a systematic review and meta-analysis.
40872801,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"Virological failure was reported in 22 of the included studies, and different virological failure thresholds were used in different studies. The pooled prevalence of virological failure was 29.46% (95% CI: 22.60 - 36.82%), and subgroup analysis using the different virological failure thresholds applied in the included studies yielded a prevalence of 24.83% (95% CI: 17.85 - 32.53%) and 36.94% (95% CI: 24.79 - 50.00%) in studies that used thresholds of >1000 copies/mL and >400 copies/mL, respectively. Meanwhile, two individual studies reported a prevalence of 57.89% (95% CI: 33.50 - 79.75%) and 8.88% (95% CI: 5.93 - 12.66%), when thresholds of >200 copies/mL and >50 copies/mL were, respectively, applied.",The paper mentions the prevalence of virological failure in studies included in the meta-analysis.
40872801,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.","The paper does not mention whether the patients were part of a clinical trial, as it is a systematic review."
40872801,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,All studies included in the systematic review were observational studies involving a total of 9685 HIV patients on ART.,"A total of 9685 HIV patients from 23 eligible studies were analyzed. The characteristics of studies that were included with their respective participants are summarized in Table 1. All included studies were observational studies, including a total of 9685 participants on ART, whereby 6677 (68.94%) were women.",The paper reports a total of 9685 HIV patients from 23 studies included in the meta-analysis.
40872801,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.",The paper focuses on studies involving patients receiving ART but does not report original sequences.
40872801,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.","The paper does not provide information on specific drug classes received by individuals, as it does not report original data."
40872801,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,No,"A systematic literature search was conducted in MEDLINE through PubMed, Embase, and CINAHL up to December 2024.",The paper does not report on specific drugs received by individuals before sample sequencing.
