40938120,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"A total of 1,159 pol gene sequences were successfully amplified.","The paper reports that pol gene sequences were successfully amplified from patient samples, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from these individuals."
40938120,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"The study assessed the prevalence, associated factors, and transmission networks of PDR among newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals in Guangxi, China, from 2019 to 2022., PDR levels and mutations were identified using the Stanford HIV Drug Resistance Database. Multivariable logistic regression models were employed to identify factors associated with PDR and to cluster the molecular network. A total of 1,048 eligible pol sequences were analyzed. The overall prevalence of PDR was 8.4%, with non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTIs) being the most commonly affected drug class. The most prevalent NNRTI-associated mutation was E138A (2.4%). High-level resistance was primarily observed to efavirenz and nevirapine. The CRF08_BC subtype exhibited significant clustering of PDR-related sequences., The pronounced clustering of PDR in the CRF08_BC subtype highlights the need for subtype-specific surveillance and intervention strategies. To improve treatment outcomes and constrain the spread of resistance, targeted educational programs on ART adherence and drug resistance awareness should be prioritized, especially among older adults and individuals infected through heterosexual contacts, alongside enhanced molecular monitoring.","The paper focuses on the prevalence and transmission networks of pretreatment drug resistance (PDR) among newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals, and does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility testing."
40938120,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,PX133190-PX134237,HIV-1 sequence data generated in this study have been deposited in GenBank and are available under accession numbers PX133190-PX134237.,The paper explicitly states that the HIV-1 sequence data generated in the study have been deposited in GenBank under the accession numbers mentioned.
40938120,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,pol gene,"An in-house RT nested PCR was used to amplify a 1,061 bp fragment of the pol gene, covering the full-length protease (PR, 99 codons) and the first 299 codons of the RT gene.","The paper mentions that the study amplified and sequenced the pol gene, which includes the protease and reverse transcriptase regions."
40938120,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,China,"A cross-sectional study was conducted between 2019 and 2022 in Nanning, Guangxi, involving 1,260 newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals with HIV.","The study was conducted in Nanning City, Guangxi, China, and all samples were obtained from this region."
40938120,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2019 to 2022,"A cross-sectional study was conducted between 2019 and 2022 in Nanning, Guangxi, involving 1,260 newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals with HIV.",The study specifically states that the data were collected between 2019 and 2022.
40938120,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"PCR products were confirmed by agarose gel electrophoresis, and positive amplicons were sequenced by Sangon Biotech (Shanghai, China) using the Applied Biosystems 3730XL Genetic Analyzer.","The paper mentions that the positive amplicons were sequenced by Sangon Biotech using the Applied Biosystems 3730XL Genetic Analyzer, which is a platform used for Sanger sequencing."
40938120,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,No evidence,The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
40938120,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma samples,"HIV-1 RNA was extracted from plasma samples using the High Pure Viral RNA Kit (Roche, Germany).",The paper specifies that HIV-1 RNA was extracted from plasma samples for sequencing.
40938120,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"A cross-sectional study was conducted between 2019 and 2022 in Nanning, Guangxi, involving 1,260 newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals with HIV., This study identified a moderate prevalence of PDR among newly diagnosed HIV patients in Guangxi, primarily driven by NNRTI-associated resistance mutations","The study focused on newly diagnosed, ART-naive individuals, meaning they had not yet started treatment and therefore had not experienced virological failure."
