40965168,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"The HIV-1 gag-protease DNA fragment from various HIV-1 isolates was cloned (pXXLAI vector), and viruses were generated by transfection. Samples with HIV-1 subtype A1, AE, AG, B, C, D, F1, G, and H were evaluated. Resistance selections in non-B subtypes led to the emergence of the same mutations with similar timeframe as in subtype B. The most prevalent capsid mutations selected across all subtypes were N74D (9 of 25 cultures), Q67H (4/25), and T107N (4/25), while M66I, K70R/S, and N74H were also observed.Patient plasma samples were obtained from studies GS-US-380-1490, GS-US-292-0104, GS-US-200-4334, and GS-US-200-4625. Patient informed consent was obtained prior to the collection of the clinical samples used in this study.","The paper discusses the sequencing of HIV-1 gag-protease DNA fragments from various clinical isolates, indicating that patient-derived samples were used for sequencing."
40965168,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,Yes,"Twenty-four clinical isolates with non-B or B HIV-1 subtype were assessed for their in vitro susceptibility to LEN and their potential to develop resistance to LEN in viral breakthrough experiments. Drug susceptibility of the HIV-1 isolates was determined in a 5-day multicycle antiviral assay in MT-2 cells using a luciferase-based viability readout.  Clinical samples with diverse HIV-1 subtypes were used to evaluate the susceptibility to LEN across these subtypes, and resistance selection with LEN in samples with various HIV-1 subtypes were conducted The overall mean LEN  \mathrm{EC}_{50}  for all viral isolates was  \[0.067\mathrm{nmol} / 1\]  (standard deviation [SD]: 0.027). HIV-1 isolates with mutant CA were evaluated for their susceptibility to LEN in 5-day multicycle phenotypic assay. CPE was assessed and measured using the luciferase-based viability cell titer glow assay. EC50 was calculated based on the percentage of inhibition compared with no drug control. % Inhibition sd  \mathrm{EC}_{50}  Fold change Inhibition at  2x  EC50 (EC50) of wild-type HIV-1 LEN isolate (XXLAI)  313234215 00Non-B HIV-1 Clinical Isolates 1S0670068380.12.002S0670068380.12.003S0670068380.12.004S0670068380.12.005S0670068380.12.006S0670068380.12.007S0670068380.12.008S0670068380.12.009S0670068380.12.010S0670068380.12.011S0670068380.12.012S06700683480.12.013S06700683480.12.014S06700683980.12.015MeanLenacapavir  1nmol/L  101.60 1.0 0 103.71 1.11.1 104.811059  1.00.0640.64 2279530.192851313.865600.0660.99 0.7lenacapavir Ec50      0.1090720.1097592.698361.3535571.3292594533120.103872      0.01 0 0 0.01 0.0906503.4 0.350521.32 0.07 0     |0.1277261116202218.23448038.5320 2028133.0245918.2 0.1096593694319532297.9   |201        22.8
