40965168,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,Yes,"The HIV-1 gag-protease DNA fragment from these plasma samples was amplified by two rounds of 30 cycles of PCR and subcloned into Zero Blunt TOPO pCR vector. The obtained vector was used to transform one shot TOP10 chemically competent cells, and colonies of interest were grown overnight.",The paper describes the process of cloning the HIV-1 gag-protease fragment into a vector before transforming into competent cells for sequencing.
40965168,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,"Plasma, cultured virus",HIV-1 RNA was extracted from 50 μl of plasma using the Mag Max-96Viral RNA isolation kit. HIV-1 DNA amplification was generated through two rounds of PCR (first round PCR primers: U563 [GCTTAAGCCTCAATAAAGCTTGCCTTG; HXB2 nucleotide (nt) 516 to 542] and RT155 [GGCCCAATTTTGAAATTTCCCTTCC; reverse complement of HXB2 nt 2678 to 2704]; second round PCR primers: U613-IF [ATCTC-TAGCAGTGGCGCCCGAACAGGGACTTGAAAG; HXB2 nt 625 to 660] and RC-5-HIV-Xma-IF [GGCCATCCATCCCGGGCTTTAATTTTACTGGTACAGTTTC; reverse complement of HXB2 nt 2565 to 2604].,"The HIV-1 RNA was extracted from plasma samples, and the sequencing involved cultured viruses derived from patient isolates."
40965168,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"The plasma samples were from participants who were treatment naive to the capsid inhibitor class, had diverse HIV-1 subtypes (A, A1, AE, AG, B, C, D, F1, G, H), and had HIV-1 RNA ranging from 3130 to 647000 copies/ml. HIV-1 subtype determination was based on the baseline protease/reverse transcriptase sequence of the participants that was analyzed prior to enrollment in the respective studies.","The paper mentions that the plasma samples were from participants who were treatment naive to the capsid inhibitor class, indicating no virological failure on a treatment regimen."
40965168,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,Yes,"Patient plasma samples were obtained from studies GS-US-380-1490, GS-US-292-0104, GS-US-200-4334, and GS-US-200-4625. Patient informed consent was obtained prior to the collection of the clinical samples used in this study.",The paper states that the patient plasma samples were obtained from specific clinical studies.
40965168,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,24,"The gag-protease DNA fragment from a total of 24 patient samples was cloned into pXXLAI, including 15 samples with non-B HIV-1 subtype and nine with HIV-1 B subtype.",The paper mentions that the gag-protease DNA fragment from a total of 24 patient samples was cloned for sequencing.
