40965168,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"The plasma samples were from participants who were treatment naive to the capsid inhibitor class, had diverse HIV-1 subtypes (A, A1, AE, AG, B, C, D, F1, G, H), and had HIV-1 RNA ranging from 3130 to 647000 copies/ml. HIV-1 subtype determination was based on the baseline protease/reverse transcriptase sequence of the participants that was analyzed prior to enrollment in the respective studies.",The paper mentions that the participants were treatment naive to the capsid inhibitor class.
