40974886,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"Protease, reverse transcriptase, integrase.","""Genotyping of protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase from 3 bictegravir/emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide switch studies was included.""","The paper explicitly mentions that genotyping of the protease, reverse transcriptase, and integrase genes was performed."
40974886,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,USA and Canada.,"""Retrospective proviral DNA genotyping of PR/RT/IN using GenoSure Archive (Monogram Biosciences, CA, USA) was performed on baseline whole blood samples and a subset of Week 24 samples (GS-US-380-4580).""","The study was conducted in accordance with the Declaration of Helsinki and included participants from designated clinical trials, which were primarily based in the United States."
40974886,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,1997 to 2019.,"""Genotypic data were available from 223 and 25 participants for the 2- and multiple-timepoint analyses, respectively (7 participants had IN data at 2 pre-switch timepoints and PR/RT data at ≥3 pre-switch timepoints and were included in both analyses). For the 2-timepoint analysis, 430 PR/RT and 140 IN reports were analyzed from 215 and 70 participants, respectively. The majority of IN reports were 1-3 years apart (69%; 48/70), and approximately half (48%; 104/215) of PR/RT reports were ≥5 years apart (Supplemental Table 2). For GS-US-380-4580, the time frame of genotypic samples was from 1.0 to 24 weeks after study drug initiation (median [Q1, Q3] 6.4 [6.0, 6.9] weeks); for GS-US-380-4030, genotypic sample time frame was from 12 to 48 weeks after study drug initiation (median [Q1, Q3] 32.9 [32.4, 33.2] weeks); and for GS-US-380-4449, samples were from Screening to 24 weeks after study drug initiation (median [Q1, Q3] 14.3 [12.5, 16.1] weeks). Overall, 241 participants (35 from GS-US-380-4449, 93 from GS-US-380-4030, and 113 from GS-US-380-4580) were included, with genotype reports collected from March 1997 to March 2019.","The text mentions that genotypic data were available from 223 and 25 participants for the 2- and multiple-timepoint analyses, respectively, and that the time frame of genotypic samples was from 1.0 to 24 weeks after study drug initiation for GS-US-380-4580, from 12 to 48 weeks for GS-US-380-4030, and from Screening to 24 weeks for GS-US-380-4449."
40974886,7,What method was used for sequencing?,"Proviral DNA, population sequencing.",Genotypic data were reported on a population sequencing level.,"The paper mentions that genotypic data were reported on a population sequencing level, indicating the method used for sequencing."
40974886,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No.,The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.,The text does not provide any information regarding cloning of samples before sequencing.
40974886,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,RNA and proviral DNA.,"""Historical RNA or proviral DNA genotype reports for protease (PR), reverse transcriptase (RT), and integrase (IN) from local laboratories or commercial sites were included.""","The paper mentions that historical RNA or proviral DNA genotype reports were included, indicating that both types of samples were sequenced."
40974886,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No.,"""The study included treatment-experienced PWH aged ≥18 years, randomized to B/F/TAF or comparator regimens in studies GS-US-380-4449 (NCT03405935 [5,6]; ≥65 years), GS-US-380-4030 (NCT03110380 [7]), and GS-US-380-4580 (NCT03631732 [8]), with virologic suppression (HIV-1 RNA <50 copies/mL) for ≥3-6 months and no prior virologic failure on integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI)-containing regimens (GS-US-380-4030, GS-US-380-4580) or no HIV-1 RNA ≥400 copies/mL (GS-US-380-4449).""",The study included treatment-experienced individuals with virologic suppression and no prior virologic failure on INSTI-containing regimens.
