40974886,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,241.,"Overall, 241 participants (35 from GS-US-380-4449, 93 from GS-US-380-4030, and 113 from GS-US-380-4580) were included, with genotype reports collected from March 1997 to March 2019.",The text states that a total of 241 participants had samples obtained for HIV sequencing.
40974886,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes.,"The study included treatment-experienced PWH aged ≥18 years, randomized to B/F/TAF or comparator regimens in studies GS-US-380-4449 (NCT03405935 [5,6]; ≥65 years), GS-US-380-4030 (NCT03110380 [7]), and GS-US-380-4580 (NCT03631732 [8]), with virologic suppression (HIV-1 RNA <50 copies/mL) for ≥3-6 months and no prior virologic failure on integrase strand transfer inhibitor (INSTI)-containing regimens (GS-US-380-4030, GS-US-380-4580) or no HIV-1 RNA ≥400 copies/mL (GS-US-380-4449).","The study included treatment-experienced individuals, meaning they had previously received ARV drugs."
40974886,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, NNRTI, PI, INSTI.","Participants were switched to B/F/TAF (bictegravir/emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide) or comparator regimens, indicating prior use of NRTIs, NNRTIs, PIs, and INSTIs.","The study involves switching to regimens that include nucleoside and nucleotide reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NRTIs), non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors (NNRTIs), protease inhibitors (PIs), and integrase strand transfer inhibitors (INSTIs)."
40974886,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"Bictegravir, emtricitabine, tenofovir alafenamide.","Participants were switched to B/F/TAF (bictegravir/emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide) or comparator regimens, indicating prior use of these specific drugs.",The study specifies that participants were switched to the bictegravir/emtricitabine/tenofovir alafenamide (B/F/TAF) regimen.
