41004608,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Clinical specimens from individuals with recently acquired HIV-1.,"Between 2015 and 2021, human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) whole genome sequencing was performed on samples from people with recently acquired HIV-1 in the United Kingdom.",The study focused on clinical specimens from individuals diagnosed with recently acquired HIV-1.
41004608,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"RITA excludes those with evidence of treatment at time of sampling, and so the sequences to which WGS was applied were strictly pretreatment.",The study excluded individuals with evidence of treatment at the time of sampling.
41004608,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"The UKHSA has sequenced HIV whole genomes from all individuals identified to have recently acquired HIV-1 in the UK since 2015 as part of routine HIV surveillance. Recent acquisition, defined as being in the preceding 6 months, is determined by the recent infection testing algorithm (RITA), which uses the results of an HIV-1 antibody avidity assay and clinical characteristics.","The paper described routine surveillance and the study of newly diagnosed individuals, not a clinical trial."
41004608,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,1182,A total of 1182 people had available WGS data between 2015 and 2021.,The paper mentioned that 1182 individuals had available whole genome sequencing data.
41004608,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"RITA excludes those with evidence of treatment at time of sampling, and so the sequences to which WGS was applied were strictly pretreatment.",The study specifically focused on sequences from treatment-naive individuals.
41004608,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"RITA excludes those with evidence of treatment at time of sampling, and so the sequences to which WGS was applied were strictly pretreatment.",The study did not report any drug classes received prior to sequencing.
41004608,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"RITA excludes those with evidence of treatment at time of sampling, and so the sequences to which WGS was applied were strictly pretreatment.","The study focused on treatment-naive individuals, and RITA excludes those with evidence of treatment at time of sampling."
41004608,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,No,"The complete genomic sequencing of HIV was performed using a previously described sequence capture method and the short read data were assembled into consensus whole genomes using Genomancer, an in-house viral genome assembly pipeline. Subtypes were obtained using the Stanford HIVdb program and the COMET HIV-1 subtyping tool. These analyses do not provide the individual patient's sequence but the consensus sequence as more protection to patient data.",The paper does not mention that individual sequences have been uploaded to any database.
