41056006,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"Resistance testing was performed for any participants who met one of the following virologic failure criteria: suboptimal virological response, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ␀e2 50 copies/mL and a decline of <1log10 from Day 1 to Week 10; virological rebound, defined as two consecutive visits with HIV-1 RNA ␀e2 50 copies/mL after reaching <50 copies/mL, or two consecutive visits with an increase from nadir of >1log10; or participants with HIV-1 RNA ␀e2 50 copies/mL at last study visit. In the Methods section, resistance is mentioned, biut it does not get into detials","The paper does not mention any in vitro drug susceptibility data, the focus was on clinical outcomes and resistance in vivo."
