41057785,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"We conducted a crosssectional study among 235 PLHIV at  the MUgH who underwent HIV drug resistance testing between 2018 and 2023, of whom 140 (59.6%) had DRMs detected, and PLHIV were predominantly on NRTI and PI based regimens, with the testing indication being mainly for second line failure. Together, these findings indicate  the  importance  of  integrating  genotype-guided  approaches  to  antiretroviral  therapy  in  this  populations.","The study involved 235 PLHIV at the MUgH who underwent HIV drug resistance testing, indicating that HIV sequences were obtained from patient samples."
