41057785,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,"NRTI, INSTI, PI, NNRTI","Table 2 Prevalence of drug resistance mutations across ART regimen drug classes DRMs were detected in 140 of 235 participants (59.6). NNRTI mutations were most prevalent at 52.8% (124/235; 95% CI: 46.4-59.2), followed by NRTI mutations at 50.2% (118/235; 95% CI: 43.8-56.6). PI major and accessory mutations were less frequent, 25.5% (60/235; 95% CI: 20.0-31.1) and 4.3% (10/235; 95% CI: 1.7-6.8), respectively. INSTI mutations were rare: 0.9% major (2/235; 95% CI: 0.3-2.0) and 0.4% accessory (1/235; 95% CI: 0.4-1.3) as shown in Table 2 below.","The study participants were on various ART regimens, predominantly involving NRTIs, NNRTIs, PIs, and some on INSTIs."
41057785,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,Not applicable,"We conducted a crosssectional study among 235 PLHIV at  the MUgH who underwent HIV drug resistance testing between 2018 and 2023, of whom 140 (59.6%) had DRMs detected, and PLHIV were predominantly on NRTI and PI based regimens, with the testing indication being mainly for second line failure. Together, these findings indicate  the  importance  of  integrating  genotype-guided  approaches  to  antiretroviral  therapy  in  this  populations.",The paper does not specify the exact drugs received by individuals prior to sample sequencing.
