41088231,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"we identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F and CRF02_AG","The paper mentions that a partial pol gene sequence was obtained from a plasma specimen collected from patient 230794, indicating that HIV sequences from patient samples were reported."
41088231,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"In conclusion, this study revealed a URF derived from subtype F2 and CRF02_AG. The recombinant structure consisted of a subtype F2 backbone and two fragments of CRF02_AG identified among HIV-infected patients in Guangdong, China. This report is the first of a full-length genome composed of these two subtypes in China, suggesting increased HIV genetic complexity in Guangdong Province. The identification of a new recombinant form may indicate the presence and transmission of several cocirculating lineages in Guangdong, possibly contributing to the emergence of new CRFs. Meanwhile, strong associations between R5/X4 HIV-1 dual tropism and fast clinical disease progression, including significantly lower CD4 cell counts, confirm the well-characterized link between X4 HIV-1 and poorer prognosis.","The paper reports genotypic drug resistance predicting genotypic co-receptor, but not in vitro drug susceptibility data."
41088231,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,PV187006,"The NFLG sequence of 230794 was 8260 nucleotides (nt) in length, and was submitted to GenBank (accession number PV187006).",The paper states that the NFLG sequence of strain 230794 was submitted to GenBank under the accession number PV187006.
41088231,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,"Near full-length genome, pol",The near full-length genome (NFLG) of HIV-1 was amplified with two overlapping segments by the near endpoint dilution method.,"The paper describes the sequencing of the near full-length genome (NFLG) of HIV-1, which includes multiple genes."
41088231,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,China,"identified one partial pol gene sequence in a plasma specimen collected from an HIV-1-infected patient, 230794, as a suspected recombinant of subtype F and CRF02_AG; Specimen 230794 was collected in Oct. 2023 from a 47-year-old man who claimed to have contracted HIV-1 through heterosexual contact in Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province, China","The paper specifies that the HIV-1 strain was identified in Guangdong, China."
41088231,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,"2023, 2025","Strain 230794 was collected in Oct. 2023 from a 47-year-old man who claimed to have contracted HIV-1 through heterosexual contact in Guangzhou City, Guangdong Province, China; Proviral DNA was extracted from the whole-blood sample collected in 2025 with the Viral DNA Extraction Kit (Supbio, China).",The paper mentions that the plasma sample was collected in October 2023 and a whole-blood sample collected in 2025.
41088231,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"Positive products were directly purified and sequenced by Sangon Biotech (Shanghai) Co., Ltd with Sanger sequencing method.",The paper states that the positive PCR products were sequenced by Sangon Biotech using the Sanger sequencing method.
41088231,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"Positive products were directly purified and sequenced by Sangon Biotech (Shanghai) Co., Ltd with Sanger sequencing method.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
