41093949,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,"No, the sequences were obtained from the HIV Sequence Database.","The HIV-1 CRF01_AE and subtype B Pol region sequences were downloaded from the HIV Sequence Database (https://www.hiv.lanl.gov/) according to the following criteria: (1) from database creation to December 31,2023; (2) country labeled as CN (China) or US (United States); (3) complete information (geographic location, year the sequence was sampled, earliest sequence taken from same subject) available; and (4) contained the Pol region.","The paper does not report sequences from patient samples directly, but rather uses sequences from the HIV Sequence Database for analysis."
41093949,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,"Yes, the paper reports in vitro drug susceptibility data.","The same RTI-induced DRMs were introduced into infectious clones of subtypes B and CRF01_AE, and phenotypic resistance tests were performed to compare the differences in susceptibilities to various RTIs. The experimental results revealed that mutations such as M41L and V106M were more likely to occur in the CRF01_AE subtype. However, phenotypic analysis of reconstructed clones containing these resistance mutations revealed that CRF01_AE exhibited significantly lower sensitivity to RTIs than did subtype B. For azvudine (FNC), a novel nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor (NRTI), the resistance level of CRF01_AE was significantly lower than that of subtype B.",The paper includes phenotypic resistance tests to compare the susceptibilities of different HIV-1 subtype strains to reverse-transcriptase inhibitors (RTIs). This indicates that in vitro drug susceptibility data was collected and reported.
41093949,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,The NCBI repository accession numbers for the AE/B recombinants are: PQ735970-PQ735985.,The NCBI repository accession numbers for the AE/B recombinants are: PQ735970-PQ735985.,The paper explicitly states the GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
41093949,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,The Pol region of HIV-1 was reported to have been sequenced.,"The HIV-1 CRF01_AE and subtype B Pol region sequences were downloaded from the HIV Sequence Database (https://www.hiv.lanl.gov/) according to the following criteria: (1) from database creation to December 31,2023; (2) country labeled as CN (China) or US (United States); (3) complete information (geographic location, year the sequence was sampled, earliest sequence taken from same subject) available; and (4) contained the Pol region.",The paper mentions the sequencing of the Pol region for the study.
41093949,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from China and the United States.,"The HIV-1 CRF01_AE and subtype B Pol region sequences were downloaded from the HIV Sequence Database (https://www.hiv.lanl.gov/) according to the following criteria: (1) from database creation to December 31,2023; (2) country labeled as CN (China) or US (United States); (3) complete information (geographic location, year the sequence was sampled, earliest sequence taken from same subject) available; and (4) contained the Pol region.",The paper specifies that the sequences were obtained from the HIV Sequence Database with the criteria of being from China or the United States.
41093949,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,The sequenced samples were obtained from 1978 to 2023.,"A total of 8654 subtype B sequences (76.36% from the USA) and 10,551 CRF01_AE sequences (0.07% from the USA) were obtained after sorting and were sampled from 1978 to 2023.","The paper states the time range from which the sequences were sampled, indicating a long history of data collection."
41093949,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing was used for sequencing.,"Positive clones were picked and amplified in LB broth containing ampicillin, followed by Sanger sequencing (by SinoGenoMax).",The paper mentions the use of Sanger sequencing for obtaining the sequences of the HIV isolates.
41093949,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,"Yes, samples were cloned prior to sequencing.","Positive clones were picked and amplified in LB broth containing ampicillin, followed by Sanger sequencing (by SinoGenoMax).","The paper describes the process of cloning, indicating that samples were cloned prior to sequencing."
41093949,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,The samples sequenced were from infectious clones of HIV-1.,"The wild-type infectious cloning pNL4-3 plasmid of HIV-1 subtype B was kindly provided by Professor Shan Lu of the University of Massachusetts Medical School, USA. The wild-type infectious cloning plasmid pGX002 of CRF01_AE is a full-length genomic infectious clone of the HIV-1 CRF01_AE strain, which was constructed by the local laboratory of the Academy of Military Medical Sciences.","The samples were sequences were from infectious clones, not directly from patient samples."
41093949,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,"No, the paper does not report sequences from individuals with virological failure.","The HIV-1 CRF01_AE and subtype B Pol region sequences were downloaded from the HIV Sequence Database (https://www.hiv.lanl.gov/) according to the following criteria: (1) from database creation to December 31,2023; (2) country labeled as CN (China) or US (United States); (3) complete information (geographic location, year the sequence was sampled, earliest sequence taken from same subject) available; and (4) contained the Pol region.",The paper does not mention any sequences were obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen.
41093949,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,"No, the study did not involve clinical trial patients.","The HIV-1 CRF01_AE and subtype B Pol region sequences were downloaded from the HIV Sequence Database (https://www.hiv.lanl.gov/) according to the following criteria: (1) from database creation to December 31,2023; (2) country labeled as CN (China) or US (United States); (3) complete information (geographic location, year the sequence was sampled, earliest sequence taken from same subject) available; and (4) contained the Pol region.","The paper does not mention whether the patients were part of a clinical trial, and focuses on sequences from the HIV Sequence Database."
41093949,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,The paper does not specify the number of individuals.,"The HIV-1 CRF01_AE and subtype B Pol region sequences were downloaded from the HIV Sequence Database (https://www.hiv.lanl.gov/) according to the following criteria: (1) from database creation to December 31,2023; (2) country labeled as CN (China) or US (United States); (3) complete information (geographic location, year the sequence was sampled, earliest sequence taken from same subject) available; and (4) contained the Pol region.",The paper does not mention the number of individuals from whom samples were obtained for sequencing.
41093949,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,The paper does not specify if sequences were from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.,"The HIV-1 CRF01_AE and subtype B Pol region sequences were downloaded from the HIV Sequence Database (https://www.hiv.lanl.gov/) according to the following criteria: (1) from database creation to December 31,2023; (2) country labeled as CN (China) or US (United States); (3) complete information (geographic location, year the sequence was sampled, earliest sequence taken from same subject) available; and (4) contained the Pol region.",The paper does not mention whether the sequences were from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs.
41093949,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,The paper does not specify drug classes received before sequencing.,"The HIV-1 CRF01_AE and subtype B Pol region sequences were downloaded from the HIV Sequence Database (https://www.hiv.lanl.gov/) according to the following criteria: (1) from database creation to December 31,2023; (2) country labeled as CN (China) or US (United States); (3) complete information (geographic location, year the sequence was sampled, earliest sequence taken from same subject) available; and (4) contained the Pol region.",The paper does not mention the drug classes received by individuals prior to sample sequencing.
41093949,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,The paper does not specify the drugs received before sequencing.,"The HIV-1 CRF01_AE and subtype B Pol region sequences were downloaded from the HIV Sequence Database (https://www.hiv.lanl.gov/) according to the following criteria: (1) from database creation to December 31,2023; (2) country labeled as CN (China) or US (United States); (3) complete information (geographic location, year the sequence was sampled, earliest sequence taken from same subject) available; and (4) contained the Pol region.",The paper does not mention specific drugs received by individuals before sample sequencing.
41093949,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,"Yes, the sequences were made publicly available.","The sequences generated during the current study are available in the NCBI repository, PQ735970-PQ735985. Additional data are available in the supplementary material.",The paper states that the sequences were made available in the NCBI repository.
41112839,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"A total of 237 samples from different patients were analyzed, and 131 (55.3%) were successfully amplified and sequenced. Among these, 14 (10.7%) harbored SDRM with significant variability across regions.","The paper reports HIV sequences from patient samples, as indicated by the number of samples analyzed and sequenced."
41112839,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"Objectives: This study aimed to document the prevalence of pretreatment drug resistance in antiretroviral therapy-naive patients in Senegal, describe mutation profiles, and evaluate their potential impact on future therapy. Methods: A pretreatment drug resistance survey was carried out in 35 sites throughout the country between 2017 and 2018 using dried blood spots and whole blood samples. Amplification and sequencing were performed on the partial reverse transcriptase (RT) gene using the Agence Nationale de Recherches sur le Sida et les hepatitis virales (ANRS: French National Agency for Research on acquired immunodeficiency syndrome [AIDS] and Viral Hepatitis)/AC11 method at the HIV National Reference Laboratory. Surveillance drug resistance mutations (SDRM) were analyzed using the Calibrated Population Resistance v8.1, and the proportion of SDRM was evaluated after grouping sites by geographical areas.",The paper focuses on a pretreatment drug resistance survey in patient samples and does not mention in vitro drug susceptibility testing or data.
41112839,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,PP280627 to PP280757,The RT-generated sequences were deposited in the National Institutes of Health GenBank database under accession numbers PP280627 to PP280757.,The paper explicitly states the GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced isolates.
41112839,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Partial reverse transcriptase (RT) gene,Amplification and sequencing were performed on the partial reverse transcriptase (RT) gene using the Agence Nationale de Recherches sur le Sida et les hepatitis virales (ANRS: French National Agency for Research on acquired immunodeficiency syndrome [AIDS] and Viral Hepatitis)/AC11 method at the HIV National Reference Laboratory.,The paper mentions that the partial reverse transcriptase (RT) gene was sequenced.
41112839,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Senegal,"Objectives: This study aimed to document the prevalence of pretreatment drug resistance in antiretroviral therapy-naive patients in Senegal, describe mutation profiles, and evaluate their potential impact on future therapy. Methods: A pretreatment drug resistance survey was carried out in 35 sites throughout the country between 2017 and 2018 using dried blood spots and whole blood samples.",The samples were obtained from a survey conducted across 35 sites in Senegal.
41112839,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2017-2018,"PDR surveillance was carried out between 2017 and 2018 according to WHO recommendations (https://apps.who.int/iris/handle/10665/204471, accessed December 2023).",The paper states that the pretreatment drug resistance survey was carried out between 2017 and 2018.
41112839,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Big Dye Terminator v3.1 sequencing and ABI 3100 Avant sequencer,"Purified and quantified polymerase chain reaction products were sequenced by using Big Dye Terminator v3.1 (Life Technologies, Courtaboeuf, France), and electrophoresis was performed on the ABI 3100 Avant sequencer (Applied Biosystems, France) as previously described [6].","The paper describes the use of Big Dye Terminator v3.1 for sequencing, with electrophoresis on an ABI 3100 Avant sequencer."
41112839,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"Amplification and sequencing were performed on the partial reverse transcriptase (RT) gene using the Agence Nationale de Recherches sur le Sida et les hepatitis virales (ANRS: French National Agency for Research on acquired immunodeficiency syndrome [AIDS] and Viral Hepatitis)/AC11 method at the HIV National Reference Laboratory. The analysis of resistance mutations was carried out using the Calibrated Population Resistance v8.1 program (https://hivdb.stanford.edu/cpr/, accessed December 2023) in search of specific mutations monitored in pretreatment.","No cloning of samples prior to sequencing is mentioned, implying direct sequencing from extracted RNA."
41112839,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Whole blood and dried blood spots,"One type of sample (dried blood spots [DBS] or venous blood) was used for each consenting patient. In Dakar (capital city), sample collection involved taking venous blood samples on ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid (EDTA) tubes from consenting patients. From 200 μl of plasma or two spots of DBS, HIV-1 viral ribonucleic acid (RNA) was extracted on the Nuclisens easyMAG® platform (Biomerieux, France) according to the manufacturer's recommendations.",The paper mentions that both whole blood and dried blood spot (DBS) samples were used for sequencing.
41112839,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,No,"The inclusion criteria for patients in the sites were to be HIV-1-positive men or women, aged at least 18, ART-naive (defined as never having received any antiretroviral therapy, including prevention of mother-to-child transmission [PMTCT] regimens), and newly diagnosed based on the patient and the healthcare provider declarations.","The study focused exclusively on antiretroviral therapy-naive individuals, and the inclusion criteria specifically defined patients as ART-naive."
41112839,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"PDR surveillance was carried out between 2017 and 2018 according to WHO recommendations (https://apps.who.int/iris/handle/10665/204471, accessed December 2023). In order to have a nationally representative sample, recruitment sites were randomly selected among those reporting more than 10 new PLHIV treated per year.","The study was a surveillance initiative to document drug resistance, not a clinical trial."
41112839,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,237 samples from different patients were analyzed,"A total of 237 samples from different patients were analyzed, and 131 (55.3%) were successfully amplified and sequenced. Among these, 14 (10.7%) harbored SDRM with significant variability across regions.",237 patient samples were analyzed in the study for HIV sequencing.
41112839,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,No,"The inclusion criteria for patients in the sites were to be HIV-1-positive men or women, aged at least 18, ART-naive (defined as never having received any antiretroviral therapy, including prevention of mother-to-child transmission [PMTCT] regimens), and newly diagnosed based on the patient and the healthcare provider declarations.","The study focused on antiretroviral therapy-naive individuals, the inclusion criteria specifically defined patients as ART-naive."
41112839,14,Which drug classes were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"The inclusion criteria for patients in the sites were to be HIV-1-positive men or women, aged at least 18, ART-naive (defined as never having received any antiretroviral therapy, including prevention of mother-to-child transmission [PMTCT] regimens), and newly diagnosed based on the patient and the healthcare provider declarations.","The study focused on treatment-naive individuals, who had not received any antiretroviral drugs before sample sequencing."
41112839,15,Which drugs were received by individuals in the study before sample sequencing?,None,"The inclusion criteria for patients in the sites were to be HIV-1-positive men or women, aged at least 18, ART-naive (defined as never having received any antiretroviral therapy, including prevention of mother-to-child transmission [PMTCT] regimens), and newly diagnosed based on the patient and the healthcare provider declarations.","The study focused on antiretroviral therapy-naive individuals, and the inclusion criteria specifically defined patients as ART-naive."
41112839,16,Were sequences from the paper made publicly available?,Yes,The RT-generated sequences were deposited in the National Institutes of Health GenBank database under accession numbers PP280627 to PP280757.,"The paper states that the sequences were deposited in the GenBank database, indicating public availability."
41129268,1,Does the paper report HIV sequences from patient samples?,Yes,"Among 333 successfully genotyped patient samples,","The paper mentions that samples were successfully genotyped, indicating that HIV sequences from patient samples were reported."
41129268,2,Does the paper report in vitro drug susceptibility data?,No,"Methods: We identified CLHIV aged 0-15 years experiencing virologic failure on first-line antiretroviral therapy (ART) in Uganda between January-November 2021 from the Central Public Health Laboratory database. Remnant viral load samples were tested for HIVDR using Sanger sequencing. Drug resistance mutations (DRMs) were identified and antiretroviral susceptibility was interpreted using the Stanford University HIVDR Database algorithms. Prevalence of DRMs and HIVDR were summarized using descriptive statistics, and associations with demographic and clinical factors were determined using chi-squared tests.","Although the paper discusses drug resistance mutations and susceptibility profiles, it does not mention in vitro drug susceptibility testing."
41129268,3,What were the GenBank accession numbers for sequenced HIV isolates?,Not reported,No evidence,The paper does not mention any GenBank accession numbers for the sequenced HIV isolates.
41129268,4,Which HIV genes were reported to have been sequenced?,Not reported,No evidence,The paper mentions the presence of drug resistance mutations but does not specify which HIV genes were sequenced.
41129268,5,From which countries were the sequenced samples obtained?,Uganda,Data for this analysis came from previously collected VL samples from children aged ≤ 15 years of age on first-line ART enrolled in any ART-accredited health facility in Uganda.,The samples were obtained from children living with HIV in Uganda.
41129268,6,From what years were the sequenced samples obtained?,2021,"Data for this analysis were obtained following the 2020 revision of the Uganda HIV Prevention, Care and Treatment Guidelines that recommended HIVDR testing for all children and adolescents living with HIV failing ART. In 2021, the Uganda Ministry of Health conducted standard-of-care HIVDR testing for CLHIV failing first-line ART to optimize treatment outcomes, through the support of the CDC-funded Faith-based Action for Scaling up Testing and Treatment for the Epidemic Response (FASTER) project.",The samples were collected between January and November 2021.
41129268,7,What method was used for sequencing?,Sanger sequencing,"Remnant viral load samples were tested for HIVDR using Sanger sequencing. Once a sample was referred to the HIVDR laboratory, clinicians received email notifications from the HIVDR Database to upload their clients' social, psychosocial, and medical profiles into the database.",The paper specifies that Sanger sequencing was used to test the samples.
41129268,8,Were samples cloned prior to sequencing?,No,"Remnant viral load samples were tested for HIVDR using Sanger sequencing. Once a sample was referred to the HIVDR laboratory, clinicians received email notifications from the HIVDR Database to upload their clients' social, psychosocial, and medical profiles into the database.",The paper does not mention any cloning of samples prior to sequencing.
41129268,9,What type of samples were sequenced?,Plasma,"Data for this analysis came from previously collected VL samples from children aged ≤ 15 years of age on first-line ART enrolled in any ART-accredited health facility in Uganda whose VL sample satisfied the following criteria: (1) sample tested for VL between January and November 2021, (2) sample type was plasma (3) VF defined as VL ≥1000 copies/mL for children on EFV or NVP or repeat VL >1000 copies/ml for children on Lopinavir/ritonavir (LPV/r) or DTG.",The paper specifies that the samples tested were plasma viral load samples.
41129268,10,Were any sequences obtained from individuals with virological failure on a treatment regimen?,Yes,"Introduction of pediatric-friendly dolutegravir (DTG) formulations to treat children living with HIV (CLHIV) has presented new opportunities to improve viral suppression; however, there are limited data on emerging patterns of HIV drug resistance (HIVDR) in this population. Methods: We identified CLHIV aged 0-15 years experiencing virologic failure on first-line antiretroviral therapy (ART) in Uganda between January-November 2021 from the Central Public Health Laboratory database. Sample from CLHIV whose prior regimen changes were made for treatment simplification or due to policy changes and not VF were classified as being on first-line ART",The paper focuses on children living with HIV experiencing virological failure on first-line antiretroviral therapy.
41129268,11,Were the patients in the study in a clinical trial?,No,"Data for this analysis came from previously collected VL samples from children aged ≤ 15 years of age on first-line ART enrolled in any ART-accredited health facility in Uganda whose VL sample satisfied the following criteria: (1) sample tested for VL between January and November 2021, (2) sample type was plasma (3) VF defined as VL ≥1000 copies/mL for children on EFV or NVP or repeat VL >1000 copies/ml for children on Lopinavir/ritonavir (LPV/r) or DTG. Repeat VL refers to a VL test taken after a child with an initial unsuppressed VL has undergone intensified adherence support for at least 3 months with 3 consecutive good adherence scores. Samples from CLHIV whose prior regimen changes were made for treatment simplification or due to policy changes and not VF were classified as being on first-line ART.",The study is based on routine data collection and standard-of-care HIVDR testing.
41129268,12,How many individuals had samples obtained for HIV sequencing?,333,"Among 333 successfully genotyped patient samples, 271 (81.4%) had any DRMs and 262 (78.7%) had any intermediate-to-high level HIVDR",The paper states that 333 samples were successfully genotyped from patients.
41129268,13,Does the paper report HIV sequences from individuals who had previously received ARV drugs?,Yes,"Data for this analysis came from previously collected VL samples from children aged ≤ 15 years of age on first-line ART enrolled in any ART-accredited health facility in Uganda whose VL sample satisfied the following criteria: (1) sample tested for VL between January and November 2021, (2) sample type was plasma (3) VF defined as VL ≥1000 copies/mL for children on EFV or NVP or repeat VL >1000 copies/ml for children on Lopinavir/ritonavir (LPV/r) or DTG. Repeat VL refers to a VL test taken after a child with an initial unsuppressed VL has undergone intensified adherence support for at least 3 months with 3 consecutive good adherence scores. Samples from CLHIV whose prior regimen changes were made for treatment simplification or due to policy changes and not VF were classified as being on first-line ART.","The paper discusses children living with HIV on first-line antiretroviral therapy, indicating prior exposure to ARV drugs."
